    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Appian Corp is a public company headquartered in McLean, Virginia, and traded under the ticker APPN. Its website describes it as providing AI-powered process orchestration across the enterprise, letting organizations orchestrate AI agents, systems, and people from a unified platform. The company says it has been automating processes for more than 25 years and that it provides AI automation for the most important business processes at the world's largest organizations.\n\nThe site groups its offering around process automation, artificial intelligence, and legacy modernization. It describes low-code building of AI-powered applications, with embedded AI agents that extract data, act autonomously, and generate code from natural language prompts. Named use cases include accounts payable and receivable, invoice processing and reconciliation, sourcing and supplier management, audit and compliance, case management, purchase-to-pay, onboarding, order intake and fulfillment, and contract review and approvals. Appian states that its onboarding automation cuts time by up to 50%. It also states that it was named a Leader in the 2025 Gartner Magic Quadrant for Business Orchestration and Automation Technologies (BOAT), and it links to an AI Value Study with Harvard Business Review Analytic Services and to a Gartner assessment of 20 BOAT vendors.\n\nCompany records give its SEC Central Index Key as 0001441683. Its recorded legal exposure is in Virginia, with a count of 152.",
